# Production-Grade Learning Management System (LMS) — 10/10 Implementation Plan

A complete, enterprise-ready technical specification and execution plan based on `LMS-Complete-Feature-Blueprint.pdf`. This plan translates the 40+ modules across 5 phases into a concrete, scalable full-stack web application architecture.

---

## System Architecture & Technical Stack

```
                          ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                          │            Client Layer (React/Next.js)      │
                          │   - Student Portal | Admin | Instructor UI    │
                          └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                                                  │ HTTPS / REST / Server Actions / WS
                                                  ▼
                          ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                          │            Next.js / API Gateway Server       │
                          │   - Auth Middleware & CSRF Protection         │
                          │   - Fine-Grained RBAC Guard (resource.action) │
                          │   - Rate Limiting (Redis / Upstash)           │
                          └─────────┬─────────────┬─────────────┬─────────┘
                                    │             │             │
               ┌────────────────────┘             │             └────────────────────┐
               ▼                                  ▼                                  ▼
   ┌───────────────────────┐          ┌───────────────────────┐          ┌───────────────────────┐
   │   Database Layer      │          │   Media & Storage     │          │  Payments & Webhooks  │
   │  PostgreSQL + Prisma  │          │ AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2│          │  Razorpay / Stripe    │
   │  (Indexing + Partition)│         │ (Pre-signed Short URLs)│         │  (Server Reconciliation)│
   └───────────────────────┘          └───────────────────────┘          └───────────────────────┘
```

### Technology Stack
- **Frontend Framework**: Next.js 14+ (App Router, Server Components & Server Actions)
- **Language & Styling**: TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI / Radix UI, Lucide Icons, Framer Motion
- **State & Data Fetching**: Zustand, TanStack Query (React Query)
- **Database & ORM**: PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM (with migrations, relational indexing, transaction locks)
- **Caching & Async Queues**: Redis / Upstash, BullMQ (for email jobs, video processing, stats rollup)
- **Media Delivery & Storage**: AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2, HLS adaptive bitrate streaming with short-lived pre-signed tokens
- **Payment Gateways**: Razorpay (India-first UPI/Cards/Netbanking), Stripe (Global Cards)
- **Authentication**: NextAuth.js / Auth.js (OAuth, Credentials, 2FA with TOTP, Session refresh token rotation)
- **Email & Notifications**: Resend / SendGrid with React Email templates

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Core Architectural Decision — Fine-Grained RBAC**:
> As specified in the blueprint, we will avoid binary `isAdmin = true/false` models. We will implement a matrix-based Permission System where permissions follow `resource.action` syntax (e.g., `course.create`, `course.publish`, `user.block`, `banner.delete`). Roles (`Super Admin`, `Admin`, `Content Manager`, `Support Staff`, `Instructor`, `Student`) will be collections of permission tokens attached to request contexts.

> [!WARNING]
> **Video Security Standard**:
> Raw media endpoints will never be exposed. All video playback will leverage private S3/R2 buckets served via time-bound (e.g., 5-minute expiry) signed URLs or tokenized HLS streaming playlists.

---

## Deferred / Features On Hold

> [!NOTE]
> 1. **Multi-Currency Dynamic Pricing**: On hold per user direction. Single base currency (e.g. INR / USD) will be used initially.
> 2. **Phase 5 Code Execution Sandbox**: On hold per user direction. Standard quiz & assignment assessments will be prioritized.

