## Infrastructure & Operating Expense Plan (AWS, DB, Media & Hosting)

A transparent cost estimate for running the LMS across development, MVP launch, growth, and scale phases.

| Category | Service Provider Options | MVP Tier (0 – 1k Active Users) | Growth Tier (1k – 10k Active Users) | Enterprise Tier (10k+ Active Users) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Relational Database (PostgreSQL)** | Managed PostgreSQL (Neon.tech / Supabase / AWS RDS) | **$0 – $19 / mo** *(Free tier / Serverless starter)* | **$50 – $150 / mo** *(Multi-AZ HA, 10GB-50GB, automatic backups)* | **$300 – $800+ / mo** *(Provisioned IOPS, Read Replicas)* |
| **Object Storage (Videos, Files, Images)** | AWS S3 vs Cloudflare R2 *(R2 highly recommended for $0 egress)* | **$0 – $10 / mo** *(R2 includes 10GB free & $0 bandwidth fee)* | **$25 – $80 / mo** *(R2 cost based on storage only, saves $200+ vs S3 egress)* | **$150 – $400 / mo** *(Multi-terabyte video library)* |
| **Video Transcoding & Streaming** | AWS MediaConvert / Cloudflare Stream / FFmpeg Workers | **$0 – $15 / mo** *(Manual HLS or lightweight worker)* | **$40 – $120 / mo** *(Automated multi-resolution HLS 1080p/720p/480p)* | **$200 – $600 / mo** *(High volume automated encoding pipeline)* |
| **Redis Cache & BullMQ Queue** | Upstash Redis / AWS ElastiCache / Redis Cloud | **$0 – $10 / mo** *(Serverless pay-per-request)* | **$30 – $70 / mo** *(High availability cluster)* | **$120 – $300 / mo** *(Dedicated memory instance)* |
| **Web Hosting & Compute API** | Vercel Pro / AWS ECS / Cloudflare Pages / Railway | **$0 – $20 / mo** *(Vercel Hobby / Pro base tier)* | **$40 – $120 / mo** *(Pro plan + serverless execution time)* | **$250 – $700 / mo** *(Autoscaling containers/ECS)* |
| **Transactional Email & SMS** | Resend / SendGrid / AWS SES | **$0 – $10 / mo** *(Resend free 3,000 emails/mo)* | **$20 – $60 / mo** *(up to 100k emails/mo)* | **$100 – $300 / mo** *(Dedicated IP)* |
| **Payment Gateway Fees** | Razorpay / Stripe | **2% (Razorpay) / 2.9% + $0.30 (Stripe)** *(Pay-per-sale)* | **Pay-per-sale** *(Volume rates negotiable)* | **Custom Enterprise rates** |
| **ESTIMATED TOTAL FIXED COST** | | **~$20 – $69 / month** | **~$205 – $610 / month** | **~$1,120 – $3,100+ / month** |

> [!TIP]
> **Cost Optimization Recommendation**:
> Using **Cloudflare R2** instead of standard AWS S3 eliminates data egress (bandwidth transfer) charges. For video-heavy LMS platforms, S3 bandwidth costs can quickly balloon to hundreds of dollars per month as students stream courses. R2 charges $0 for egress, keeping monthly infrastructure under $70 during MVP/Growth phases.


## Proposed Implementation Phases & Module Breakdown

---

### Phase 1: MVP & Core Foundations (Launch Readiness)

#### 1. Identity, Auth & Fine-Grained RBAC
- **User Authentication**:
  - Email/password signup with bcrypt hashing & email verification token workflow.
  - OAuth 2.0 (Google, GitHub, Apple).
  - Password reset with secure time-limited tokens.
  - Session management with JWT refresh token rotation & revocation tracking in Redis.
  - Optional 2FA TOTP (Authenticator apps) for privileged accounts.
- **Database Schema**:
  - `User`, `Account`, `Session`, `Role`, `Permission`, `RolePermission`, `UserRole`, `AuditLog`.

#### 2. User & Admin Dashboards
- **Student Dashboard**:
  - "Continue Learning" banner with last-watched position resume CTA.
  - Enrolled courses grid with completion progress bars.
  - Earned certificates library.
  - Wishlist & purchase history tab.
  - Real-time learning stats (total hours, daily active streak).
- **Admin Dashboard**:
  - Key Platform KPIs (Total users, published vs draft courses, sales summary).
  - Quick action shortcuts.

#### 3. Granular User Management (Admin)
- Paginated user list with full-text search by name/email, role filtering, status filters.
- Admin actions: Create user, edit profile, block/unblock, force password reset, change role assignments.
- Deep user snapshot: Enrolled courses, completion stats, order history, audit activity log.

#### 4. Course & Curriculum Management (Admin)
- **Course Hierarchy**: Course -> Section -> Lesson (Atomic content unit).
- **Course CRUD**:
  - Metadata: Title, subtitle, description, thumbnail, preview video, category/subcategory, tags, difficulty, language, pricing.
  - Tree-view Curriculum Builder: Drag-and-drop section/lesson reordering, lesson content types (Video, PDF, Rich Text/HTML, Quiz).
  - Course States: `Draft`, `Pending Approval`, `Published`, `Unpublished`, `Rejected`, `Archived`.

#### 5. Secure Video Learning System
- Player features: Speed control (0.5x–2x), quality selector, caption/subtitle tracks, PiP, keyboard shortcuts, auto-play next lesson.
- Video Security: Private Cloudflare R2 / AWS S3 storage, pre-signed expiring stream URLs, server-side entitlement validation per request.
- Auto-save watch position every 10 seconds to compute exact watch percentage & auto-mark completion at 90%.

#### 6. Quiz & Certificate Engine
- **Quiz System**:
  - Question types: Single choice, multiple answer, True/False, Fill in the blank, Matching pairs.
  - Configurations: Pass %, time limit, max attempts allowed, randomized question order, per-question explanations.
  - Instant scoring screen with detailed answer reviews.
- **Certificate System**:
  - Automatic PDF generation upon 100% course completion.
  - Unique Certificate ID, public verification link (`/verify/[certificateId]`), and QR code embedding.

---

### Phase 2: E-Commerce, Payments & Financial Engine

#### 1. Cart, Checkout & Multi-Gateway Integration
- **Shopping Cart**: Dynamic cart overlay and dedicated page with tax/discount calculation.
- **Checkout Process**:
  - **Razorpay**: Native SDK checkout integration for India (UPI, Netbanking, Cards).
  - **Stripe**: Hosted & embedded payment element for global credit card processing.
- **Strict Server-Side Verification**: Webhook handlers (`payment.captured`, `checkout.session.completed`) cryptographically verify signatures before unlocking course access in database transactions.

#### 2. Coupons, Discounts & Invoicing
- **Coupon System**: Percentage off, fixed amount, course-specific or category-wide scope, usage caps, per-user limits, expiry dates.
- **Invoice Generation**: Automated PDF creation with itemized breakdown, tax/GST registration info, and download links in student dashboard.
- **Refund Workflow**: Student submission -> Admin review & approval -> Automated gateway refund trigger -> Revocation of enrollment.

---

### Phase 3: Multi-Instructor Platform & Social Learning

#### 1. Instructor System & Payouts
- Instructor application & approval workflow.
- Custom commission rate configuration per instructor.
- Dedicated Instructor Portal: Course authoring, student analytics, earnings statements, payout requests.
- Payout Engine: Automated earnings calculation after platform fee deduction.

#### 2. Ratings, Reviews & Lesson Q&A
- **Ratings & Reviews**: 1–5 star reviews with text feedback, star distribution chart, admin moderation queue for flagged reviews.
- **Lesson Q&A**: Threaded Q&A tab under video player, instructor verified badges, "Mark as Accepted Answer", upvoting.
- **Wishlist & Price Alerts**: One-click save to wishlist, dynamic notifications on price drops or promotional sales.
- **Notifications**: Multi-channel delivery (In-app bell menu + transactional emails).

---

### Phase 4: CMS, SEO, Marketing & System Operations

#### 1. Homepage & Content Management System (CMS)
- CMS-Driven Homepage: Admin-configurable hero banner, featured categories grid, dynamic course carousels, testimonials section, customizable footer & FAQ.
- Media Library: Platform-wide asset storage with MIME type validation, thumbnail generation, and alt-text SEO tagging.
- Pages Management: Rich text editor for static pages (About Us, Terms, Privacy Policy, Refund Policy).

#### 2. Blog Engine & SEO Suite
- **Blog Management**: Post creation with categories, tags, cover image, author profiles, scheduled publishing.
- **SEO Enhancements**: Structured JSON-LD schema (Course schema), auto-generated `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`, custom meta titles/descriptions, OpenGraph social preview tags.

#### 3. Affiliate System & Operations
- **Affiliate/Referral**: Unique referral link generator, conversion tracking cookies, commission dashboard.
- **Support Tickets**: Ticket submission (Payment, Tech, Content), admin assignment, status updates, attachments.
- **Audit Logs**: Tamper-evident admin action logging (User ID, IP address, timestamp, action type, resource diff).

---

### Phase 5: AI Features, Coding Sandbox & Mobile Ecosystem

#### 1. AI Learning Assistant & AI Quiz Generator
- Contextual AI Assistant: RAG-based chatbot answering student questions using video transcript embeddings.
- AI Quiz Generator: Automated generation of quizzes from lesson summaries.

#### 2. In-Browser Sandboxed Coding Exercises
- Embedded Monaco Editor (VS Code core) with syntax highlighting.
- Sandboxed Code Execution: Multi-language runner (Python, JavaScript, Java, C++) executing against test cases with pass/fail outputs.

#### 3. Gamification & Mobile Readiness
- Daily login & learning streaks, achievement badges, global course leaderboards.
- Cross-platform API endpoints designed for React Native / Flutter mobile clients.

---

## Complete Database ERD Schema Structure (Prisma)

```prisma
// Core Tables Overview
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

model User {
  id            String          @id @default(cuid())
  name          String?
  email         String          @unique
  passwordHash  String?
  image         String?
  role          UserRoleEnum    @default(STUDENT)
  isBlocked     Boolean         @default(false)
  userRoles     UserRole[]
  enrollments   Enrollment[]
  progress      LessonProgress[]
  quizAttempts  QuizAttempt[]
  certificates  Certificate[]
  orders        Order[]
  reviews       Review[]
  questions     Question[]
  answers       Answer[]
  auditLogs     AuditLog[]
  createdAt     DateTime        @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime        @updatedAt
}

model Role {
  id          String           @id @default(cuid())
  name        String           @unique
  description String?
  permissions RolePermission[]
  userRoles   UserRole[]
}

model Permission {
  id          String           @id @default(cuid())
  action      String           @unique // e.g. "course.publish"
  description String?
  roles       RolePermission[]
}

model RolePermission {
  roleId       String
  permissionId String
  role         Role       @relation(fields: [roleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  permission   Permission @relation(fields: [permissionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@id([roleId, permissionId])
}

model UserRole {
  userId String
  roleId String
  user   User   @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  role   Role   @relation(fields: [roleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@id([userId, roleId])
}

model Course {
  id            String         @id @default(cuid())
  title         String
  slug          String         @unique
  subtitle      String?
  description   String?
  thumbnail     String?
  previewVideo  String?
  price         Decimal        @db.Decimal(10, 2)
  discountPrice Decimal?       @db.Decimal(10, 2)
  status        CourseStatus   @default(DRAFT)
  level         CourseLevel    @default(BEGINNER)
  language      String         @default("English")
  categoryId    String
  category      Category       @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id])
  sections      Section[]
  enrollments   Enrollment[]
  reviews       Review[]
  createdAt     DateTime       @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime       @updatedAt
}

model Section {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  title       String
  order       Int
  courseId    String
  course      Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  lessons     Lesson[]
}

model Lesson {
  id          String           @id @default(cuid())
  title       String
  order       Int
  contentType LessonType       @default(VIDEO)
  videoUrl    String?
  duration    Int?             // seconds
  isFree      Boolean          @default(false)
  sectionId   String
  section     Section          @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  progress    LessonProgress[]
  quizzes     Quiz[]
  questions   Question[]
}

model Enrollment {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId    String
  courseId  String
  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  course    Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@unique([userId, courseId])
}

model LessonProgress {
  id             String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId         String
  lessonId       String
  isCompleted    Boolean  @default(false)
  watchTimeSec   Int      @default(0)
  lastPositionSec Int     @default(0)
  user           User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  lesson         Lesson   @relation(fields: [lessonId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@unique([userId, lessonId])
}

enum UserRoleEnum {
  SUPER_ADMIN
  ADMIN
  CONTENT_MANAGER
  SUPPORT_STAFF
  INSTRUCTOR
  STUDENT
}

enum CourseStatus {
  DRAFT
  PENDING_APPROVAL
  PUBLISHED
  UNPUBLISHED
  REJECTED
  ARCHIVED
}

enum CourseLevel {
  BEGINNER
  INTERMEDIATE
  ADVANCED
  ALL_LEVELS
}

enum LessonType {
  VIDEO
  PDF
  TEXT
  QUIZ
  ASSIGNMENT
  CODING
}
```

---

## Verification & Testing Strategy

### 1. Automated Testing Suite
- **Unit & Integration Tests (Vitest & Supertest)**:
  - Test permission evaluation engine with mock users and permission sets.
  - Test shopping cart, coupon application, and tax calculation functions.
  - Test webhook signature validation logic for Razorpay & Stripe.
- **End-to-End Tests (Playwright)**:
  - Full student journey: Registration -> Browse course -> Add to cart -> Checkout simulation -> Access course video player -> Complete quiz -> Download certificate.
  - Admin journey: Login -> Create course tree -> Upload video -> Publish course -> Verify user permissions.

### 2. Manual Security & Performance Verification
- **Video Access Verification**: Attempt direct URL fetch of video files without authentication headers to confirm private bucket access control.
- **RBAC Guard Test**: Attempt cross-role API calls (e.g., Student hitting `/api/admin/users`) to verify immediate 403 Forbidden responses.
- **Lighthouse Performance Audit**: Verify PageSpeed performance, SEO metadata, dynamic OpenGraph tags, and mobile accessibility scores >= 90.
